The outbound network-containment path in egress — the transparent forward proxy,
host allowlist, connect-time CIDR deny, DNS interception and rebinding guard,
TLS MITM / SNI passthrough, the credential-transform pipeline (AWS SigV4, HMAC,
OAuth2, GCP tokens), header allowlist, MCP interception and response retry — is
derived from iron-proxy. It lives under internal/ and gen/, with the module path
rewritten to github.com/hanzoai/egress and its control, secret and audit surfaces
replaced by Hanzo IAM, Hanzo KMS and the Hanzo event bus.

